<!-- 20C (2F), Jill on the second mansion visit: Yawn's rematch and the
     pass number.

     Until scenario 0x27 is set, Yawn 2 (entity 0x12, enemy bit 0x3E) lies
     dormant with no aim bit. Pressing AOT 2 by the west wall (on_aot_02)
     plays its entrance and sets 0x27; on later entries it waits by the
     door. While it lives, the hole's AOT 3 is armed with no trigger; once
     it is dead room main arms it for the action button. Pressing it
     (on_aot_03) shows "It's too dark to see anything.", sets common 0x26,
     plays Barry's scene and drops Jill into the pit at (22400,4000).

     In the pit, event_1B sets room flag 0x0A after 600 frames, and room
     main then runs from_main_2: Barry comes back with the rope, sets common
     0x25 (the pass number for 201's keypad) and hands over the radio and
     the pass-number file (AOT 7 and 8, zones at the origin). The timer
     lives in the room's event task, so leaving by the ladder first loses
     it: the bot waits for 0x25 before anything else.

     With rope=leave the bot gets out first. The pit's AOT 6 floor probe
     sets room flag 0x3E; with it set, AOT 4 at the ladder hatch asks
     "There's a switch below. Will you push it?", and Yes slides the cover
     off (scenario 0x28) and arms AOT 10 in the same zone as door 1 to
     21A: "There's a ladder. Will you descend it?", whose Yes turns the
     door on. The planner then takes door 1, the pit's only way out
     without the rope (21A is a room not yet entered), and its press
     there answers the ladder's prompt. On seed 1 the bot is down the
     ladder about 170 frames after the fall, well inside the 600-frame
     timer, so Barry never comes back with the rope and 0x25 stays clear.

     Door 1 to 21A stands on the pit floor: from 20B's side of the room it
     is out of reach, and the pit can be entered only once (the dark hole,
     after Yawn 2). The <reach> keeps the planner from walking back to it
     on any other entry.

     Chris's game: the same pit is his way down to 21A (and on through
     21B and 21C to the 200 lift, his only way into 213 to 219 on the
     second visit, and 110). His AOT 3 is armed with no trigger until Yawn
     2 is dead; then room main arms it for the action button, and
     examine_pit's Yes drops him in at (23100,4100) with no flag set. The
     passage check takes it once it is live (door 1 to 21A has no
     approach from this side), and the switch below the hatch and the
     ladder down then work as for Jill. So Yawn's entrance (AOT 2) and the
     fight come first: without them the bot reached 20C with an empty
     gun, found the hole dead and the ladder door out of reach, and went
     back and forth through 20B until the frontier ran out. 21A holds the
     ladder back up shut for him (21A's notes). -->
<bot format="2">
  <interact slot="2" bank="0" bit="0x27" character="jill" label="wake Yawn by the west wall"/>
  <interact slot="2" bank="0" bit="0x27" character="chris" label="wake Yawn by the west wall"/>
  <fight enemy="0x12" bank="3" bit="0x3E" character="chris"
         label="Yawn 2: its death arms the dark hole, Chris's way down to 21A"/>
  <fight enemy="0x12" bank="3" bit="0x3E" character="jill" label="Yawn 2"/>
  <interact slot="3" bank="1" bit="0x26" character="jill" label="the dark hole"/>
  <wait bank="1" bit="0x25" after_bank="1" after_bit="0x26" character="jill"
        when="rope=wait" label="Barry's rope"/>
  <interact slot="4" bank="0" bit="0x28" after_bank="1" after_bit="0x26" character="jill"
            when="rope=leave" label="the switch below the hatch"/>
  <reach slot="1" bank="1" bit="0x26" while="set" entry="same" character="jill"
         label="the ladder door to 21A stands in the pit: Yawn 2 dead, then down the dark hole"/>
</bot>
